# Movies API requests - a Postman collection you keep in Git, next to the code.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), then click
# "Send Request" above any request. Run them top to bottom: the create request
# names its response "created", and the ones after it reuse that _id.
# Prefer Postman? Import movies-api.postman_collection.json instead.

@api = http://localhost:3001/api
@matrix = 573a139bf29313caabcf3d23

### ---------- READ ----------

### Search by title (any case, part of the title)
GET {{api}}/movies?title=matrix

### Filter by genre and year
GET {{api}}/movies?genre=Sci-Fi&year=1999

### Pagination: page 3, 5 per page
GET {{api}}/movies?genre=Western&page=3&limit=5

### One movie, every field
GET {{api}}/movies/{{matrix}}

### ---------- CREATE ----------

# @name created
POST {{api}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "INET2005: The Movie",
  "year": 2026,
  "runtime": 95,
  "genres": ["Documentary", "Comedy"],
  "rated": "PG",
  "plot": "Students build an API in an afternoon.",
  "directors": ["A. Student"]
}

### Read it back
GET {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}

### ---------- UPDATE ----------

### PATCH: change only these fields
PATCH {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rated": "PG-13", "runtime": 102 }

### PUT: replace the whole movie - plot, genres, directors are gone afterwards
PUT {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "INET2005: The Director's Cut", "year": 2027 }

### ---------- DELETE ----------

DELETE {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}

### Gone: 404
GET {{api}}/movies/{{created.response.body.$._id}}

### ---------- THINGS THAT SHOULD FAIL ----------

### 400: breaks the schema (no title, year too early)
POST {{api}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "year": 1066 }

### 400: not an ObjectId
GET {{api}}/movies/banana

### 404: a valid id that isn't in the collection
GET {{api}}/movies/000000000000000000000000

### 400: body isn't valid JSON
POST {{api}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{ title: oops }
